From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] comgr: give unbundling a distinct cache action ID

LLVM 24 no longer exposes OffloadUnbundlingJobClass. This value is only
used to distinguish cache keys, so allocate a COMGR-specific class after
the driver actions and the existing SPIR-V class.

--- a/amd/comgr/src/comgr-unbundle-command.cpp
+++ b/amd/comgr/src/comgr-unbundle-command.cpp
@@ -121,7 +121,9 @@
 }

 CachedCommandAdaptor::ActionClass UnbundleCommand::getClass() const {
-  return clang::driver::Action::OffloadUnbundlingJobClass;
+  // LLVM removed the driver unbundling action. Reserve a COMGR cache class
+  // after the driver actions and the SPIR-V class (JobClassLast + 1).
+  return clang::driver::Action::JobClassLast + 2;
 }

 void UnbundleCommand::addOptionsIdentifier(HashAlgorithm &H) const {
